---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **K팝 팀이 봉우리를 지나고 나서 얼마나 남는가.** (`/group-afterlife`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 오늘 이슈(2026-09-07): 「BigBang is back … why the K-pop group still matters」
 *   「still matters」는 주장이다. 우리는 그것을 «수»로 낸다 —
 *   가장 읽히던 달과 지금을 나란히 놓으면 된다.
 *
 * ⭐ 그리고 이 축은 이슈가 식어도 남는다. 어느 팀이 컴백하든 같은 표에 얹힌다.
 *   사장님 지시(2026-09-06): 「이슈+롱테일」 — 이슈로 데려오고 축으로 남긴다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 팀에 등수를 매겨 「한물갔다」고 안 쓴다. 나란히 놓고 수만 적는다
 * ⛔ 「위키백과를 덜 찾는다」를 「인기가 없다」로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다
 * ⛔ 못 잰 73팀을 0 으로 안 채운다 — 몇 팀인지 화면에 적는다 (자료를 847팀으로 넓혀 46→73)
 * ⛔ 🔴 봉우리가 «지난달»인 팀을 「안 꺼진 팀」으로 자랑하지 않는다.
 *    꺼질 시간이 없었을 뿐이다. 그래서 «봉우리 뒤 12개월 이상» 지난 것만 따로 센다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-group-afterlife.json';

const TITLE = 'How long a K-pop group stays looked up after its peak';
const DESC =
  'For 774 Korean acts, the median time to lose half the readers of their best month is '
  + 'two months. One group held out for 65. Peak month, month by month, both sides counted.';

const 셈 = d.셈;
const 큰 = d.팀.filter((t) => t.봉우리열람 >= 50000);
const 느린 = 큰.filter((t) => Number.isFinite(t.반토막까지개월))
  .sort((a, b) => b.반토막까지개월 - a.반토막까지개월).slice(0, 12);
const 가장큰봉우리 = [...d.팀].sort((a, b) => b.봉우리열람 - a.봉우리열람).slice(0, 12);
/* ⭐ 「아직 안 꺼졌다」는 봉우리 뒤 «시간이 있었을 때»만 뜻이 있다 */
const 오래버틴 = d.팀.filter((t) => t.반토막안됨 && t.봉우리뒤개월 >= 12)
  .sort((a, b) => b.봉우리뒤개월 - a.봉우리뒤개월);
const 아직오르는중 = d.팀.filter((t) => t.반토막안됨 && t.봉우리뒤개월 === 0).length;

/* ⛔ 창이 2015-07 부터라 그 앞에 데뷔한 팀은 «진짜 봉우리»를 못 본다.
   그래서 「언제 봉우리가 오나」는 2016년 이후 데뷔 팀만으로 답한다. 나머지는 «뺀다». */
const 데뷔있음 = d.팀.filter((t) => Number.isFinite(t.데뷔해) && t.데뷔해 >= 1990 && t.데뷔해 <= 2024);
const 창안쪽 = 데뷔있음.filter((t) => t.데뷔해 >= 2016);
const 데뷔격차 = (t) => Number(t.봉우리달.slice(0, 4)) - t.데뷔해;

const 중앙값 = (a) => {
  const s = [...a].filter(Number.isFinite).sort((x, y) => x - y);
  if (!s.length) return null;
  return s.length % 2 ? s[(s.length - 1) / 2] : +((s[s.length / 2 - 1] + s[s.length / 2]) / 2).toFixed(1);
};
const 세대들 = [1990, 1995, 2000, 2005, 2010, 2015, 2020].map((b) => {
  const g = 데뷔있음.filter((t) => t.데뷔해 >= b && t.데뷔해 <= b + 4);
  return { 띠: `${b}–${b + 4}`, 수: g.length, 중앙: 중앙값(g.map((t) => t.반토막까지개월)) };
});

const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 위키 = (t) => `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(String(t).split(' ').join('_'))}`;
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} page="/group-afterlife">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Every Korean act has one month when more people looked it up than in any other. We found
    that month for <b>{셈.잰팀} of them</b> and counted what was left afterwards. The median
    act fell below half of its best month within <b>{셈.반토막까지중앙값개월} months</b>.
  </p>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The whole set</h2>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Korean acts with an English Wikipedia article</td><td>{수(셈.받은팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Measured here (at least 24 months of data)</td><td><b>{수(셈.잰팀)}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Dropped for too few months — <i>not counted as zero</i></td><td>{수(셈.못잰팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Have fallen below half their peak month</td><td>{수(셈.반토막된팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Median months from peak to half</td><td><b>{셈.반토막까지중앙값개월}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Have not fallen below half yet</td><td>{수(셈.아직안꺼진팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>…of which peaked <i>this month</i>, so had no time to fall</td><td>{아직오르는중}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      That last line matters. An act whose best month is the most recent month cannot have
      declined yet, and counting it as durable would be wrong. Only
      {' '}<b>{오래버틴.length}</b> acts have gone twelve months or more past their peak and
      still hold half of it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Held on longest — acts whose peak month drew 50,000 or more</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Restricted to the {큰.length} acts with a peak of at least 50,000 reads, so that a small
      article with noisy months cannot lead the table.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Act</th><th>Months from peak to half</th><th>Peak month</th><th>Peak reads</th><th>Left today</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {느린.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="noopener">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td><b>{t.반토막까지개월}</b></td>
            <td>{t.봉우리달}</td>
            <td>{수(t.봉우리열람)}</td>
            <td>{t.남은몫}%</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      The gap between first and second place is the finding here, not the ranking itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The largest peaks, and what is left of them</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Act</th><th>Peak month</th><th>Peak reads</th><th>Latest month</th><th>Left</th><th>Peak to half</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {가장큰봉우리.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="noopener">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.봉우리달}</td>
            <td>{수(t.봉우리열람)}</td>
            <td>{수(t.요즘열람)}</td>
            <td>{t.남은몫}%</td>
            <td>{t.반토막까지개월 == null ? 'not yet' : `${t.반토막까지개월} mo`}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      A very large peak does not buy a slow decline. Several of the biggest months in this
      table were an act's debut or a single event, and the month after was already half.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Past their peak by a year or more, and still above half</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Act</th><th>Peak month</th><th>Months since</th><th>Left</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {오래버틴.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="noopener">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.봉우리달}</td>
            <td>{t.봉우리뒤개월}</td>
            <td>{t.남은몫}%</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Most of this list is not idol pop. Several are rock and indie acts whose readership was
      never large enough to spike, and a flat line never has a peak to fall from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>When the peak arrives</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Our reads begin in July 2015, so for an act that debuted earlier we cannot know whether
      its real peak came before we were looking. This table therefore uses only the
      {' '}<b>{창안쪽.length}</b> acts that debuted in 2016 or later, whose whole career sits
      inside the window. The other {데뷔있음.length - 창안쪽.length} acts with a known debut year
      are left out of this question rather than given a peak we cannot verify.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Gap between debut year and peak month</th><th>Acts</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {[['Peaked in the debut year itself', 0, 0],
          ['One to two years later', 1, 2],
          ['Three to five years later', 3, 5],
          ['Six years or more', 6, 99]].map(([이름, 아래, 위]) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{이름}</td>
            <td>{창안쪽.filter((t) => 데뷔격차(t) >= (아래 === 0 ? -99 : 아래) && 데뷔격차(t) <= 위).length}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      The median gap is <b>two years</b>. Fewer than one act in six had its biggest month in
      the year it debuted, and the tail runs long — some acts do not reach their best month
      for six years or more.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The fall has not changed in thirty years</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Debut years</th><th>Acts</th><th>Median months from peak to half</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {세대들.map((c) => (
          <tr><td>{c.띠}</td><td>{c.수}</td><td>{c.중앙 ?? '—'}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      For acts that debuted before 2016 this is the fall from their highest month
      <i>inside our window</i>, which need not be their career high — but the descent is
      measured the same way for every act, and it does not vary by generation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Korean <i>titles</i> lose half their reading in about the same two months —
      {' '}<a href="/half-life">we measured that separately</a>, on a different unit, and the
      timescale came out the same. Comics run the other way:
      {' '}<a href="/webtoon-adaptations">a Korean webtoon is read 14 times more</a> once a
      drama exists, so an adaptation builds attention where a comeback mostly spends it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/group-afterlife" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Acts and debut years — Wikidata SPARQL (P31/P279* Q215380 <i>musical group</i>,
      P495 <i>country of origin</i> Q884). Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews REST API, English
      Wikipedia, all-access, <b>agent=user</b> (bots excluded), monthly, {d.창}. The current
      month is excluded because it is not finished. Collected {d.잰때}.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
